{
  "uid": "meizuno-apps",
  "title": "Meizuno — Apps",
  "description": "Per app: requests by route (count, p50/p95, errors), the process's CPU and memory, its logs, and CPU/memory profiles by function. Provisioned from git — edit grafana/dashboards/meizuno-apps.json, because the file overrides UI changes on reload.",
  "tags": [
    "meizuno",
    "provisioned"
  ],
  "editable": true,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "1m",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "timezone": "browser",
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "app",
        "label": "App",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "victoriametrics"
        },
        "definition": "label_values({__name__=~\"python_info|nodejs_version_info\"}, job)",
        "query": {
          "query": "label_values({__name__=~\"python_info|nodejs_version_info\"}, job)",
          "refId": "app"
        },
        "refresh": 2,
        "sort": 1,
        "includeAll": false,
        "multi": false,
        "description": "An app with its own /metrics (port 9000): a job that reports its runtime, python_info or nodejs_version_info. Its Pyroscope service_name and its Loki service label are the same name."
      },
      {
        "name": "cpu_profile",
        "type": "query",
        "hide": 2,
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "victoriametrics"
        },
        "definition": "query_result(label_set(python_info{job=\"$app\"}, \"profile\", \"process_cpu:cpu:nanoseconds:cpu:nanoseconds\") or label_set(nodejs_version_info{job=\"$app\"}, \"profile\", \"wall:cpu:nanoseconds:wall:nanoseconds\"))",
        "query": {
          "query": "query_result(label_set(python_info{job=\"$app\"}, \"profile\", \"process_cpu:cpu:nanoseconds:cpu:nanoseconds\") or label_set(nodejs_version_info{job=\"$app\"}, \"profile\", \"wall:cpu:nanoseconds:wall:nanoseconds\"))",
          "refId": "cpu_profile"
        },
        "regex": "/profile=\"([^\"]+)\"/",
        "refresh": 2,
        "includeAll": false,
        "multi": false,
        "description": "Pyroscope's CPU profile type for the app's SDK: Python's pyroscope-io and Node's @pyroscope/nodejs name it differently."
      },
      {
        "name": "inuse_profile",
        "type": "query",
        "hide": 2,
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "victoriametrics"
        },
        "definition": "query_result(label_set(python_info{job=\"$app\"}, \"profile\", \"memory:inuse_space:bytes:space:bytes\") or label_set(nodejs_version_info{job=\"$app\"}, \"profile\", \"memory:inuse_space:bytes:inuse_space:bytes\"))",
        "query": {
          "query": "query_result(label_set(python_info{job=\"$app\"}, \"profile\", \"memory:inuse_space:bytes:space:bytes\") or label_set(nodejs_version_info{job=\"$app\"}, \"profile\", \"memory:inuse_space:bytes:inuse_space:bytes\"))",
          "refId": "inuse_profile"
        },
        "regex": "/profile=\"([^\"]+)\"/",
        "refresh": 2,
        "includeAll": false,
        "multi": false,
        "description": "Pyroscope's memory-in-use profile type for the app's SDK: Python's pyroscope-io and Node's @pyroscope/nodejs name it differently."
      },
      {
        "name": "level",
        "label": "Log level",
        "type": "custom",
        "query": "critical,error,warn,info,debug,unknown",
        "options": [],
        "current": {
          "text": [
            "All"
          ],
          "value": [
            "$__all"
          ]
        },
        "multi": true,
        "includeAll": true,
        "allValue": ".+",
        "description": "Loki's detected_level. Filters the Logs row only."
      },
      {
        "name": "search",
        "label": "Log search",
        "type": "textbox",
        "query": "",
        "current": {
          "text": "",
          "value": ""
        },
        "description": "Plain text, any case. Filters the Logs row only."
      }
    ]
  },
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "How to read this",
      "collapsed": true,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "panels": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "title": "How to read this",
          "gridPos": {
            "h": 27,
            "w": 24,
            "x": 0,
            "y": 1
          },
          "options": {
            "mode": "markdown",
            "content": "## What this dashboard shows\n\nPick an app above. Everything here comes from the app itself: its own `/metrics` (port 9000, scraped every 30 s) and the profiles it pushes to Pyroscope. Rates are 5-minute averages; the stats and the table cover the whole selected time range and count every request from the container's start (`increase_pure`), so they are exact right after a deploy too.\n\n| Term | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **Duration** | Measured inside the app, from the request arriving to the **last byte** of the answer. A stream counts whole: English's session stream includes the model writing the exercises, a Forma assistant turn includes the model's reply. Traefik's latency on the overview adds the network in front. |\n| **route** | The declared route template, e.g. `/api/v1/shared/{public_id}/day`, or `/api/transactions/:id` in money-manager — never the real path, which can carry a credential. `static` is the built client's files, `unmatched` is anything no route matched (404s). money-manager renders pages on the server: `page` is one of them, and its 404s are pages too. The health check is not counted. |\n| **p50 / p95** | Line a route's requests up from fastest to slowest: p50 is the one in the middle (the typical request), p95 the one 95% of them beat (how bad the slow ones get). Estimated from histogram buckets (5, 10, 25, 50, 100, 250, 500 ms, 1, 2.5, 5, 10, 30, 60 s), so `17.5 ms` means *somewhere between 10 and 25 ms*. With only a few requests, p95 is simply the slowest. |\n| **Total time** | Requests × their average duration — exact, not estimated. The table is sorted by it: where the server's time went. |\n| **status** | A class: `2xx`, `3xx`, `4xx`, `5xx`. `none` means no response was ever started — an unhandled error on its way to a 500, or a client that left first. |\n| **CPU** | % of **one** core. Limits: english 0.5 core (50%), forma 2 cores (200%), money-manager 1 core (100%). |\n| **Memory** | Resident memory of the app's process (Python, or Node for money-manager). Every app is limited to 512 MiB; above it the container is OOM-killed. |\n| **instance** | One per container. During `docker rollout` two exist for a moment, so per-instance panels briefly show both. |\n\n## Logs\n\nThe app's own output, from every container it ran in during the range — a rollout's old container included. **Log level** and **Log search** above filter both panels; the search is plain text, any case.\n\n- **level** is Loki's `detected_level`. Forma's JSON lines carry their own; English's and uvicorn's text lines get it from their `ERROR:` / `WARNING:` prefix (Alloy reads it). `unknown` is a line with no level at all — in Forma mostly httpx's `HTTP Request: …`, and the text copy of a traceback whose JSON line is already under error.\n- An English traceback is **one** entry, under the `ERROR:` line that announced it. Forma logs a crash as one JSON line, `unhandled_error`, with the traceback in its `exception` field.\n- Click a line for its fields; **Show context** gives the lines around it.\n\n## Profiles (bottom row)\n\n- **CPU by function** — where CPU time went, summed over every request in the range. Only time **on** the CPU: a request awaiting Postgres or OpenAI is on no stack while it waits, so \"slow because waiting\" shows in Duration and not here. For money-manager (Node) it is the CPU time of wall-clock samples — the same thing, measured another way. Its `Non JS threads activity` is CPU spent on the process's other threads: Prisma's query engine, V8's garbage-collector and compiler helpers, Node's I/O pool.\n- **Memory allocated by function** — bytes allocated during the range: who churns memory. Python apps only — Node's heap profiler keeps no record of memory already freed.\n- **Memory in use by function** — sampled heap still held: who keeps memory. A leak grows here.\n- Click a frame to zoom. **Explore → Pyroscope** can diff two time ranges."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Requests in range (count)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "victoriametrics"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 5,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(increase_pure(http_request_duration_seconds_count{job=\"$app\"}[$__range]))",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "blue",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "graphMode": "none",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "description": "Every request except the health check, over the selected range."
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "p95 duration in range (s)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "victoriametrics"
      },
